      "description": "answer the scope-changing questions: the principal holding scope.answer (a person, or a decider at the autonomy levels that grant it) accepts each default or changes it, and its answers are recorded with that principal; moves the questions to a new revision; not once the interview is settled. Admissible on an interview whose shape is not checked yet (r6): the person's own edit of an answer moves the questions to a revision no check has seen, and scope.answer is what takes that edit; questions.check runs on the revision it writes. Not on an interview found invalid.",
      "effect": "write",
      "executor": {
        "bound": true,
        "kind": "person",
        "max_runs": 8,
        "program": "sdc-tool.sh scope-answer {principal}"
      },
